     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for the answer Tareef, is there any work around in this situation that you would indicate?<span><br><br>On Thursday, October 8, 2015 at 8:19:52 AM UTC-3, Tareef Kawaf wrote:</span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">Unfortunately <a href=\"http://shinaypps.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinaypps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362659639000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wxj1e4xXcIGITUNC90ihE\">shinaypps.io</a> doesn&#39;t have support for Oracle today.  It requires local drivers to be installed and we have avoided all non open source databases. We may have to reconsider that if there is sufficient demand for it however.<div><br></div><div><br></div></div></span><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><span>On Thu, Oct 8, 2015 at 7:07 AM, Lucas Augusto <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">lucasd...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>I&#39;m currently developing an Shiny App which connects to an Oracle Database in the company I work at. </div><div>The app is working like a charm locally, however when I try to deploy it through ShinyApp.io it starts by installing all the packages and when it gets to <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ROracle/ROracle.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ROracle/ROracle.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362659639000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1z81kvDOM__P_C2Pd8-WUw\">ROracle </a>package it returns the following error:<br><div style=\"bo